.TH CHANGELOG-PREVIEW 8 "July 2026" "changelog 1.0.0" "System Administration Commands"
.SH NAME
changelog preview \- render fragment changes as colored markdown output for terminal display
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B changelog preview
[\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
The \fBpreview\fR command renders accumulated fragment changes as formatted, colorized markdown suitable for terminal viewing. It provides a visual representation of what release notes will look like without actually generating files or performing archiving operations.

This is useful for reviewing changes before releasing, checking formatting consistency, and getting a quick overview of recent work across multiple fragments.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Show help message and exit.

.TP
\fB-d\fR, \fB\-\-dir\fR=\fIPATH\fR
Fragment directory to render. Defaults to "changelogs/fragments" in the current project root. Can specify multiple directories using separate -d flags or comma-separated paths.

.TP
\fB-n\fR, \fB\-\-notes-dir\fR=\fIDIR\fR
Additional fragment directories to merge into the preview output. Useful for viewing fragments organized by subsystem or team alongside main fragments.
.SH OUTPUT FORMATTING
.PP
The preview command applies ANSI color codes for enhanced terminal readability:

.TP
.B Header Styling:
.RS 4
.IP \(bu 2
\fIH1 headers (## [Version])\fR → Bold yellow
.IP \(bu 2
\fIH2 headers (### Category)\fR → Bold cyan
.IP \(bu 2
\fIH3+ headers\fR → Bold white
.RE

.TP
.B Link Styling:
.RS 4
.IP \(bu 2
\fIMarkdown links [text](url)\fR → Cyan underline
.IP \(bu 2
\fIBold link text **text**\fR → Bright green bold
.RE

.TP
.B Bullet List Markers:
.RS 4
.IP \(bu 2
\fI- or * list items\fR → Yellow bullet marker with indented content
.IP \(bu 2
\fINested lists\fR → Hierarchical indentation preserved
.RE

.TP
.B Code Blocks:
.RS 4
.IP \(bu 2
\fIFenced code blocks (```) \fR→ Dim gray background
.IP \(bu 2
\fIInline code (`text`)\fR → Highlighted with backticks preserved
.RE

.SH TERMINAL COMPATIBILITY
.PP
The preview command automatically detects terminal capabilities:

.RS 4
.IP \(bu 2
\fITty detection:\fR Checks if stdout is an interactive terminal using \fBisatty()\fR
.IP \(bu 2
\fIColor support:\fR Disables ANSI codes when piping to files or non-terminal destinations
.IP \(bu 2
\fIBackground processing:\fR Safe for use in CI/CD pipelines without color interference
.RE

.TP
.B When colors are disabled:
.RS 4
.IP \(bu 2
Output is plain markdown suitable for file redirection
.IP \(bu 2
No ANSI escape sequences in piped output
.IP \(bu 2
Maintains proper formatting and structure
.RE

.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Preview current fragments with default settings:
.nf
    changelog preview
.fi

.TP
View fragments from multiple directories:
.nf
    changelog preview \\
        -d changelogs/fragments/core \\
        -n changelogs/notes/community \\
        -n changelogs/fragments/plugins
.fi

.TP
Pipe output to file for review:
.nf
    changelog preview > /tmp/changelog-preview.md
    less /tmp/changelog-preview.md
.fi

.TP
Use with grep for specific changes:
.nf
    changelog preview | grep -i "bugfix\|enhancement"
.fi

.SH SEE ALSO
.TP
\fBchangelog-release(8)\fR \- Generate actual release notes (preview shows what will be created)
.TP
\fBchangelog-log(8)\fR \- Display fragments in git-log style format
.TP
\fBless(1)\fR, \fBmore(1)\fR \- Terminal paging utilities for viewing large outputs
